\item Reverse edge  which are incident to node $k$

\item Remove any 2-cycles formed by step 1. 


\end{enumerate}


The quiver with $n$ nodes can be encoded into $n\times n$ skew-symmetric matrix, $B\in \Mat(\mathbb{Z}) $ in which each entry $b_{ij}$ represents the number of edges from $i$ to $j$ i.e.
\begin{center}
