\subsection{Execution}
Execution is the operational core of urban LLM agents, translating high-level reasoning into concrete actions. Achieving this goal requires a robust framework capable of functioning under real-world constraints. We categorize existing research into three execution modes: (1) \emph{single-agent execution}, where an individual agent perceives and acts autonomously; (2) \emph{multi-agent collaboration}, where multiple agents coordinate across distributed urban environments; and (3) \emph{human-agent collaboration}, where agents interact with human stakeholders through dialogue, feedback, and shared decision-making.

