Unlike before, all split points $h_j$, $j=1,\ldots,k$, are now included in the interior of another seMCD-bucket. All  points between $h_1$ and $h_k$, that are not split points, are included in the interior of two different seMCD-buckets. In all cases, the algorithm will output one of the correct seMCD-buckets, or in exceptional cases their intersection, with the same guarantees as before. 

