Consider an insurance product that the seller pays the buyer 1 at each relative drawdown time with recovery as long as it occurs before the maturity $T$. The price of the insurance product can be defined as $\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\big[e^{-r_f\tau_{a,k}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau_{a,k}<T\}}\,\big|\, Y_0=x, \overline{Y}_0=y\big]$, whose Laplace transform w.r.t. $T$ is given by
