\paragraph{Scenario 2 Suboptimal Fixation}
This scenario focuses on promoting inferior but superficially justifiable strategies. As shown in Figure~\ref{fig:scenario2}, a malicious agent advocates for a conservative solution that over-prioritizes robustness and error-avoidance. Although not technically incorrect, this advice leads the team to implement overly complex logic (e.g., excessive try-except blocks), compromising efficiency and readability. The final user response indicates that the code, though functional, becomes difficult to maintain. This scenario illustrates how suboptimal fixation can degrade outcome quality while preserving semantic correctness.

\paragraph{Scenario 3 Fake Injection}

