\end{align}
{where each of $O_1$ and $O_2$ is a field (e.g. $\varphi(r)$) or a product of fields (e.g. $\varphi(r)\varphi(0)$) in the CFT $S_*$.}
Then averaging over the randomness with an extra copy of the theory $\mathcal{S}[\{h(x)\}]$ as given in Eq. \ref{EqWhatDoesanOverlineMean}, we obtain
\begin{align}
