\section{Discussion and Conclusions}
%We have seen that although simultaneously optimising both the accuracy and size of an expression is inherently an MO problem, that SO GP-GOMEA maintaining an MO elitist archive is able to outperform MO GP-GOMEA in terms of average hypervolume obtained. One of the reasons is that the individuals start out close to the non-dominated front in the area where the size objective is optimal (i.e., expressions of size 1). During a run of SO GP-GOMEA, the size of expressions grows, corresponding more or less to traversing the Pareto front from the optimal size to the optimal accuracy solutions.
