\section{Data} \label{sec:data}
This work leverages the stellar parameters and abundances from the Milky Way Mapper (MWM) (J. A. Johnson et al., {\em in prep}) survey as part of the 5th iteration of the Sloan Digital Sky Survey (SDSS-V; Kollmeier et al., {\em submitted}) as well as positional and kinematic data from the ESA \gaia mission \citep{gaia_tot}. By combining data from only two sources we create a uniform sample that minimizes any systematic offsets which arise when data is pulled from multiple sources. 

\subsection{SDSS-V/MWM DR19}

The 19th data release from SDSS-V (DR19; Aghakhanloo et al., {\em submitted}) includes chemical abundances and radial velocities from MWM for $\sim 1$ million stars. 
