\subsection{Galactic Trends for Other Elements}\label{all_elems}

\subsubsection{$\alpha-$Elements -- O, Mg, Si, S, Ca, Ti}\label{alpha}

We show the [$\alpha$/Fe] abundance gradients for six $\alpha$-elements (O, Mg, Si, S, Ca, Ti) with respect to \rguide in Figure \ref{fig:alpha}. We find shallow positive slopes for Mg and S. 
O, Si, and Ca all display gradients consistent with no trend.  
%In both this work and in \natp~we find positive slopes for O, however, the trend was much stronger in \natp~($0.012$ dex kpc$^{-1}$) and not consistent within the error. 
In Ti, we find a negative slope, in contrast to the flat or slightly positive gradients the rest of the alpha elements display. 
%which are inconsistent with the positive slopes found in \natp. 
We do note that the Ti abundances show a larger scatter than the other elements considered here. Ti abundances consistently exhibit larger scatter in APOGEE spectra, regardless of the abundance determination method employed (\citealt{Souto2019}, \citealt{Jonsson2020}).
% in both from the DR17-based \natp~and this work. We also determine the gradient for these elements with respect to \rgc and both sets of gradients are recorded in Table \ref{tab:gradients}. 
The gradients determined with respect to \rgc and \rguide are in good agreement with each other, with no significant differences. 

